## 📌 Key Insights

- TRANSFER transactions exhibited the highest fraud rate across all transaction channels.
- Fraudulent activity represented only ~0.11% of total transactions, reflecting highly imbalanced real-world financial datasets.
- Alert prioritization reduced investigation scope to less than 0.2% of customers.
- Fraud exposure was heavily concentrated within high-value transfer and cash-out transactions.
- Risk scoring enabled operational prioritization of suspicious entities and transactions.

